    <!-- https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlsOntology#ISOControl -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlsOntology#ISOControl">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKCube#Control"/>
        <terms:contributor>Junli Liang</terms:contributor>
        <terms:contributor>Rob Brennan</terms:contributor>
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-05-08</terms:created>
        <terms:source>ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)</terms:source>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An ISO control is defined as a measure that modifies or maintains risk. Some of the controls in this document are controls that modify risk, while others maintain risk. An information security policy, for example, can only maintain risk, whereas compliance with the information security policy can modify risk.  Moreover, some controls describe the same generic measure in different risk contexts. This document provides a generic mixture of organizational, people, physical and technological information security controls derived from internationally recognized best practices.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlsOntology#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ISO Control</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ISO control is defined as a measure that modifies or maintains risk. Some of the controls in this document are controls that modify risk, while others maintain risk. An information security policy, for example, can only maintain risk, whereas compliance with the information security policy can modify risk.  Moreover, some controls describe the same generic measure in different risk contexts. This document provides a generic mixture of organizational, people, physical and technological information security controls derived from internationally recognized best practices.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ISO Control</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


